# Holodisk from the Brotherhood Library
# uses the global var BROTHERHOOD_LIBRARY_DISK

{2000}{}{Vault Locations v34.129 Revision C (Western USA)}
{2001}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2002}{}{Hello, and welcome to the latest edition of the Western}
{2003}{}{United States Vault Location Pamphlet. We hope you}
{2004}{}{enjoy the pamphlet, and remember Vaults are not just}
{2005}{}{for the upwardly mobile, but for everyone.}
{2006}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2007}{}{Vault 12}
{2008}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2009}{}{Under the sprawling metropolis of Bakersfield, lies the}
{2010}{}{technological magnificence of Vault 12. Built with every}
{2011}{}{amenity in mind for the prospective Vault Dweller,}
{2012}{}{Vault 12 was given the "Pressed Vault Suit"}
{2013}{}{award for attention to preparedness. Buried far}
{2014}{}{underground, the protection that Vault Dwellers will}
{2015}{}{receive will be unprecedented. Much like all other}
{2016}{}{Vaults, Vault 12 has been fitted with the newest in}
{2017}{}{Vault Water Purification Systems. Able to take even}
{2018}{}{the waste located in the sewers of Bakersfield, this}
{2019}{}{system is able to deliver over 15,000 gallons of pure,}
{2020}{}{refreshing drinking water every day.}
{2021}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2022}{}{Vault 13}
{2023}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2024}{}{Located in a scenic mountainous region northwest of}
{2025}{}{Vault 12, this Vault offers an endless supply of pure}
{2026}{}{water to the inhabitants. The rumors that the water}
{2027}{}{table in the area could easily be contaminated in the}
{2028}{}{event of a Nuclear War have been found by the}
{2029}{}{Department of Water and Power to be completely}
{2030}{}{unfounded. In the event that the water in the area}
{2031}{}{were to become tainted, remote even though it may be,}
{2032}{}{Vault 13 has been fitted with the government approved}
{2033}{}{Vault Water Purification System. Rated to work without}
{2034}{}{significant loss of output for over 250,000 hours,}
{2035}{}{prospective Vault Dwellers should have nothing to fear.}
{2036}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2037}{}{Vault 15}
{2038}{}{**END-PAR**}
#
{2039}{}{Due east from Vault 13, construction on this Vault has}
{2040}{}{gone extremely smoothly. Much work was done to}
{2041}{}{reinforce the walls of the third level of this Vault, to}
{2042}{}{make all the future Vault Dwellers more secure in the}
{2043}{}{knowledge that in the event of even a major earthquake,}
{2044}{}{the regulatory computers of the Vault would continue}
{2045}{}{to function. Recent tours of the newly constructed}
{2046}{}{Vault, have had many a potential Vault Dweller walking}
{2047}{}{away with a new found awe of the improvements done to}
{2048}{}{this already impressive Vault.}
{2049}{}{**END-DISK**}



# *** Brotherhood of Steel Honor Code ***
# *** Maxson's History ***
{3000}{}{My father was a security guard at a secret military base}
{3001}{}{in the desert of southern California. A typical MP, I}
{3002}{}{remember mostly his strength. When it came time for}
{3003}{}{the revolution, I respected his convictions. He stayed}
{3004}{}{behind, to help those who were disabled and wounded,}
{3005}{}{even the scis. He put the well being of myself and my}
{3006}{}{mother into the hands of his best friend, and ordered}
{3007}{}{us into the desert with the other rebels.}
{3008}{}{**END-PAR**}
# -
{3009}{}{We, very few, marched into the wastes. The only thought}
{3010}{}{on my mind was that I would never see my father again.}
{3011}{}{He knew that to stay behind was death. And still, he}
{3012}{}{stayed. He respected the flag, the CIC and the badge}
{3013}{}{that he wore.}
{3014}{}{**END-PAR**}
# -
{3015}{}{What an idiot.}
{3016}{}{**END-PAR**}
# -
{3017}{}{He died for the sins of others. That will never happen}
{3018}{}{again to us. We will become self-sufficient. We will}
{3019}{}{become keepers of knowledge and lore. We will survive}
{3020}{}{the end of civilization. We will take responsibility}
{3021}{}{for our actions, and we will hold accountable the}
{3022}{}{actions of others.}
{3023}{}{**END-PAR**}
# -
{3024}{}{This I pledge to you, Maxson, my son. The Brotherhood}
{3025}{}{of Steel is justly named. We are a Brotherhood. Unlike}
{3026}{}{my father, we will stand back to back with those that}
{3027}{}{share our convictions and beliefs. We are Steel. We are}
{3028}{}{hard. We have been sharpened to and edge.}
{3029}{}{**END-PAR**}
# -
{3030}{}{Always remember the fires that we were forged in.}
{3031}{}{Never forget. }
{3032}{}{The motto from a previous time, and our motto now.}
{3033}{}{**END-DISK**}
# Survival Recipes
{4000}{}{VDSG - APPENDIX 6: SURVIVAL RECIPES}
{4001}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4002}{}{Mushroom Clouds}
{4003}{}{(preheat oven to 200 degrees Fahrenheit / 90 degrees }
{4004}{}{Celsius)}
{4005}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4006}{}{3-4 egg whites (at room temperature) }
{4007}{}{1/4 teaspoon cream of tartar}
{4008}{}{1 cup superfine sugar*}
{4009}{}{cocoa}
{4010}{}{8 oz / 200 g dark chocolate (bittersweet or semi-sweet)}
{4011}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4012}{}{Beat the eggs and tartar with an electric mixer until }
{4013}{}{soft peaks form. Add the sugar a little at a time while }
{4014}{}{continuing to beat, until all the sugar is in and the }
{4015}{}{mixture is glossy and stiff.}
{4016}{}{Using a piping bag with a no. 8 tip, pipe out an equal }
{4017}{}{number of caps and stems onto an ungreased non-stick }
{4018}{}{cookie sheet. The caps should be about the diameter of a }
{4019}{}{quarter, and the stems should be about an inch high and }
{4020}{}{the diameter of a soda straw.}
{4021}{}{Sprinkle cocoa over the caps and stems, and then}
{4022}{}{blow on them to spread out the cocoa more evenly. You}
{4023}{}{may want to do this outside, as cocoa goes everywhere.}
{4024}{}{Bake for 2 hours at 200 F / 90 C.}
{4025}{}{Carefully remove the caps and stems from the}
{4026}{}{cookie sheet. With a dull knife, snip the top of each}
{4027}{}{stem so it has a flat top surface.}
{4028}{}{Melt the chocolate (in a double boiler or microwave). }
{4029}{}{Spread the chocolate on the base of each cap }
{4030}{}{with a butter knife or spatula, and use it to glue a }
{4031}{}{stem in place. Put the assembled mushrooms in the }
{4032}{}{refrigerator for 20 minutes to harden the chocolate, }
{4033}{}{then put them in an airtight container.}
{4034}{}{Makes 3-4 dozen.}
{4035}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4036}{}{Desert Salad}
{4037}{}{(Increase or reduce ingredient portions to taste)}
{4038}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4039}{}{1 lb / 500 g extra lean ground beef}
{4040}{}{(turkey may be substituted)}
{4041}{}{1/2 head of iceberg lettuce, cut}
{4042}{}{3 oz / 100 g pinto beans}
{4043}{}{6 oz / 200 g sliced olives}
{4044}{}{4 oz / 150 g cheddar cheese}
{4045}{}{6 oz / 200 g tortilla chips}
{4046}{}{1 firm tomato}
{4047}{}{1 16 oz / 500 ml bottle of Catalina dressing}
{4048}{}{1 avocado (optional)}
{4049}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4050}{}{Brown the meat, drain.}
{4051}{}{In large bowl, mix lettuce, beans, and olives. Crush }
{4052}{}{chips and add. Cut tomato into small chunks and add to }
{4053}{}{bowl. Shred cheese and add. Slice avocado and add. Add}
{4054}{}{meat. Toss with dressing. Serve.}
{4055}{}{Makes 4-6 portions.}
{4056}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4057}{}{*superfine sugar is NOT confectioner's sugar or 10X sugar. }
{4058}{}{If you cannot find superfine sugar, it's easy to make. Just }
{4059}{}{put granulated sugar in a blender or food processor, and }
{4060}{}{blend for 1 minute.}
{4061}{}{**END-PAR**}
{4062}{}{Bon Appetit,}
{4063}{}{Timothy Cain, your Vault Chef}
{4064}{}{**END-PAR**}
