{9000}{}{In the year 2067, Senator Todd Peterson decided to }
{9001}{}{build a secret bunker to house himself and his family }
{9002}{}{should war break out. Senator Peterson was a }
{9003}{}{wealthy man in his own right, but lacked the funds }
{9004}{}{necessary for such a project. Through secret }
{9005}{}{dealings with Poseidon Oil and a covert branch of the }
{9006}{}{government known as the Enclave, the final funding }
{9007}{}{for the project was attained. A construction sight }
{9008}{}{was chosen in southern Colorado and work began.}
{9009}{}{**END-PAR**}
{9010}{}{Ten years after the construction was completed, war }
{9011}{}{did indeed break out. Senator Peterson was in }
{9012}{}{Washington DC at the time and, much to his chagrin, }
{9013}{}{was taken completely by surprise. The senator made }
{9014}{}{a desperate attempt to gather his family and reach the }
{9015}{}{bunker, but his small plane never arrived. The bunker }
{9016}{}{might have remained lost were it not for a surviving }
{9017}{}{member of the senator's family, Ben Schilling.}
{9018}{}{**END-PAR**}
{9019}{}{In the year 2077, Captain Roger Maxson left the }
{9020}{}{Mariposa military base and traveled to the secret Lost }
{9021}{}{Hills bunker for the purpose of establishing a new }
{9022}{}{military order. He brought with him a loyal group of }
{9023}{}{followers consisting of both military personnel and }
{9024}{}{scientists. Among these was Corporal Ben Shilling. }
{9025}{}{It was at this time that Maxson established the }
{9026}{}{Brotherhood of Steel. As the Brotherhood grew they }
{9027}{}{began to look into the possibility of expanding their }
{9028}{}{operations. It was then that Ben Schilling revealed }
{9029}{}{the location of the Senator Peterson's bunker. The }
{9030}{}{location was filed for future use.}
{9031}{}{**END-PAR**}
{9032}{}{In the year 2231, Jeremy Maxson, was leading a }
{9033}{}{thriving Brotherhood of Steel. Jeremy decided that it }
{9034}{}{was time to expand BOS operations into the east. He }
{9035}{}{sent an expeditionary force composed of five paladins }
{9036}{}{to confirm the location of Peterson's bunker. The }
{9037}{}{expedition leader, Andrea Brixley, discovered the }
{9038}{}{bunker, disabled its security, and opened it for }
{9039}{}{habitation. For over a decade she and her fellow }
{9040}{}{paladins explored the east and forged relationships }
{9041}{}{with many of the tribes that inhabited the area.}
{9042}{}{**END-PAR**}
{9043}{}{In the year 2242, Jeremy Maxson renamed the bunker }
{9044}{}{after his famous ancestor, Roger Maxson. He then }
{9045}{}{sent a full compliment of troops for occupation. }
{9046}{}{Andrea Brixley was promoted to Elder, given the rank }
{9047}{}{of General, and placed in charge. The remainder of }
{9048}{}{her exploratory team was given the title of Elder as }
{9049}{}{well. It was not long afterward that the war with the }
{9050}{}{New California Republic was announced.}
{9051}{}{**END-PAR**}
{9052}{}{- Chronicler Elder Paladin Glenn Deering}
{9053}{}{**END-DISK**}
# -
{10000}{}{I began my career in the Brotherhood as a scribe but got }
{10001}{}{tired of the technical side of life. I asked to be }
{10002}{}{placed in a combat role and was given the chance to }
{10003}{}{prove myself. I was found to be a competent combatant }
{10004}{}{who also had the advantage of being able to repair }
{10005}{}{equipment on the fly in the field. I worked }
{10006}{}{my way up the ranks and soon earned the title of Elder.}
{10007}{}{**END-PAR**}
{10008}{}{I am a headstrong no holds barred kind of woman. I am }
{10009}{}{opinionated, I know it, and I don't care. I will often voice }
{10010}{}{my opinion tactlessly whether or not it is asked for. }
{10011}{}{Considered a bitch by most anyone who knows me }
{10012}{}{and I could not care less. As someone once said, }
{10013}{}{well-behaved women seldom make history.}
{10014}{}{**END-PAR**}
{10015}{}{- An Abbreviated Autobiography}
{10016}{}{- Elder Paladin Traci Niels, January 3rd, 2253}
{10017}{}{**END-DISK**}
