{12000}{}{NEW CALIFORNIA REPUBLIC INFORMATION DISK 1}
{12001}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12002}{}{We're Here! Why not join us?}
{12003}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12004}{}{There's a wonderful future ahead - and it could be   }
{12005}{}{yours with the New California Republic!}
{12006}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12007}{}{But what is it, you want to know?}
{12008}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12009}{}{HOW BIG IS NCR?}
{12010}{}{Founded eighty years ago, the NCR is now comprised of }
{12011}{}{the states of Shady, Los Angeles, Maxson, Hub, and    }
{12012}{}{Dayglow.  Approximately 700,000 citizens are pleased  }
{12013}{}{to call NCR home.}
{12014}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12015}{}{WHAT DOES NCR STAND FOR?}
{12016}{}{The New California Republic is dedicated to bringing  }
{12017}{}{peace, security and justice to the people of the great}
{12018}{}{west.  NCR's fine police forces constantly patrol and }
{12019}{}{arrest any raiders, cannibals, slavers, and lawless  }
{12020}{}{mutants within the country, and the NCR Army valiantly}
{12021}{}{protects the borders against outside marauders. To    }
{12022}{}{ensure justice and liberty, all citizens have access  }
{12023}{}{to NCR's courts and the right to vote for a           }
{12024}{}{representative of their choice to sit in the Hall of  }
{12025}{}{Congress. In the words of President Tandi,            }
{12026}{}{"A safe people is a strong people."}
{12027}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12028}{}{WHO'S IN CHARGE HERE?}
{12029}{}{NCR may be a bit different from what you're used to.  }
{12030}{}{There are no chieftains, town bosses, kings, or       }
{12031}{}{dictators here. Our leaders are elected by the people!}
{12032}{}{That's right -- every state has the right to send     }
{12033}{}{representatives to the Hall of Congress. These        }
{12034}{}{representatives select the President and              }
{12035}{}{Vice-President to head the council and it is their    }
{12036}{}{advice which guides the President's decisions.  For   }
{12037}{}{ten terms now, President Tandi has been the unanimous }
{12038}{}{choice of the council, who respect her wisdom and     }
{12039}{}{foresight.                                            }
{12040}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12041}{}{SOUNDS GREAT! HOW DO I JOIN THE NCR?}
{12042}{}{All law-abiding and peaceful people, human or mutant, }
{12043}{}{are eligible to become citizens of NCR. To become a   }
{12044}{}{citizen all you have to do is move to NCR and present }
{12045}{}{your claim for immigration. After citizenship training}
{12046}{}{and processing your application,  you will be notified}
{12047}{}{of your new status as a PC (Provisional Citizen). From}
{12048}{}{there, it's only a short step to full citizenship!}
{12049}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12050}{}{Of course, NCR is not for everybody - slavers,        }
{12051}{}{unreformed mutants, known raiders, and other          }
{12052}{}{undesirables need not apply!                          }
{12053}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12054}{}{BUT I WHAT IF MY ENTIRE TOWN WANTS TO JOIN?}
{12055}{}{Depending on where your town is located, NCR does     }
{12056}{}{accept petitions by villages, towns, bases,           }
{12057}{}{city-states, even minor kingdoms for annexation by    }
{12058}{}{NCR. Once the petition is accepted, NCR will grant    }
{12059}{}{your town territorial status. Once the needed police  }
{12060}{}{and army presence is established and any banditry or  }
{12061}{}{other lawlessness has been dealt with, your village   }
{12062}{}{can apply for full statehood in the NCR. It's that    }
{12063}{}{simple!}
{12064}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12065}{}{So remember - WE'RE HERE. WHY NOT JOIN US?}
{12066}{}{**END-PAR**}
{12067}{}{Prepared by the New California Relations Advisory Panel}
{12068}{}{**END-PAR**}
