# State of the Nation
{13000}{}{Memo: State of the Nation}
{13001}{}{From: President Dick Richardson}
{13002}{}{To: The People of this Great Nation}
{13003}{}{Subject: The State of the Union Address}
{13004}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13005}{}{Fellow Americans, I have been honored to be the steward}
{13006}{}{that will take the American people back to the mainland}
{13007}{}{to reclaim the United States for its own citizens. We }
{13008}{}{will be the first generation free of the mutant threat }
{13009}{}{in over one hundred years.}
{13010}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13011}{}{It's been a long wait, and the work that has made this }
{13012}{}{possible has been difficult. At times it seemed }
{13013}{}{impossible, however through the brave and tireless }
{13014}{}{efforts of our own head of the Chemical Corps, Dr. }
{13015}{}{Charles Curling, the hour of our salvation is now at }
{13016}{}{hand.}
{13017}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13018}{}{Brave, steadfast, blah, blah, blah. Jeez, does anyone }
{13019}{}{really listen to this stuff?}
{13020}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13021}{}{--Notes to self-}
{13022}{}{1)  Go on like this for a bit to cover Curling's project.}
{13023}{}{2)  Tell everyone how steadfast, etc., they are}
{13024}{}{     Yadda, yadda, yadda}
{13025}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13026}{}{Be sure to make a plug for reelection.}
{13027}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13028}{}{Remember NOT to hug my intern on the way down from the}
{13029}{}{podium.}
{13030}{}{**END-PAR**}
{13031}{}{Important: Finish writing this soon. We'll be able to }
