# Circle of Steel Diary
{14000}{}{[Begin holodisk record]}
{14001}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14002}{}{Entry #1:}
{14003}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14004}{}{Our path has been decided, and the cause is noble. We }
{14005}{}{were Brotherhood once, but now we are more. We are the }
{14006}{}{Circle of Steel, formed from the ashes of betrayal. We've }
{14007}{}{salvaged the Stealth Boys, the tech our former leaders }
{14008}{}{shunned due to baseless fears of mental side effects.}
{14009}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14010}{}{Entry #8:}
{14011}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14012}{}{The Stealth Boys, they're remarkable. The invisible veil they }
{14013}{}{cast, it's like slipping into another world. We're }
{14014}{}{shadows now, infiltrating NCR territories, collecting }
{14015}{}{vital intel. But the Brotherhood...they're watching, I can }
{14016}{}{feel it. }
{14017}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14018}{}{Entry #15:}
{14019}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14020}{}{We are besieged on all sides. The NCR, the Brotherhood, }
{14021}{}{they're closing in. But our cause is just, our methods are }
{14022}{}{sound. We shall prevail. The Stealth Boys protect us, }
{14023}{}{they make us untouchable. But the shadows... they're }
{14024}{}{longer now. Darker. Can a shadow cast a shadow?}
{14025}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14026}{}{Entry #21:}
{14027}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14028}{}{Whispers in the dark. Voices that are not there. Images }
{14029}{}{that fade when I turn to see them. Are these the side }
{14030}{}{effects the Brotherhood feared? No. No, they're tricks, }
{14031}{}{deceptions, smoke screens cast by our enemies. We're not }
{14032}{}{the sick ones...they are.}
{14033}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14034}{}{Entry #26:}
{14035}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14036}{}{The walls of our bunker are closing in. Betrayal breeds }
{14037}{}{in every corner, every shadow. Are we not all Circle of }
{14038}{}{Steel? Can I trust no one? They whisper about me, plot }
{14039}{}{against me, I know it. The Stealth Boys, they are our }
{14040}{}{salvation, our curse. But who am I without my shadow?}
{14041}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14042}{}{Entry #32:}
{14043}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14044}{}{Who's there? I see you, skulking in the corners of my sight. }
{14045}{}{My mind? The Brotherhood... traitors! The Stealth Boys, }
{14046}{}{they stole them, stole my mind. Or was it me? Was it }
{14047}{}{us? I can't...I can't remember. We were supposed to be }
{14048}{}{the heroes...}
{14049}{}{**END-PAR**}
{14050}{}{[End holodisk record]}
{14051}{}{**END-DISK**}
# Project Chimera
{15000}{}{WARNING! Access to this diary is restricted. Any }
{15001}{}{unauthorized attempt to access or disseminate its }
{15002}{}{contents will result in severe consequences.}
{15003}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15004}{}{ENTRY #1}
{15005}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15006}{}{DATE: Classified}
{15007}{}{LOCATION: S1C}
{15008}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15009}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15010}{}{Today marks the beginning of Project Chimera, a }
{15011}{}{clandestine endeavor shrouded in secrecy. Our mission: }
{15012}{}{to push the boundaries of genetic experimentation for }
{15013}{}{military purposes. The laboratory hums with }
{15014}{}{anticipation as we embark on this historic journey.}
{15015}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15016}{}{ENTRY #2}
{15017}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15018}{}{DATE: Classified}
{15019}{}{LOCATION: S1C}
{15020}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15021}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15022}{}{Progress is swift as we delve deeper into the }
{15023}{}{intricacies of genetic cherry-picking. Our experiments }
{15024}{}{yield promising results, with specimens exhibiting }
{15025}{}{remarkable adaptability to diverse environments. The }
{15026}{}{potential for military application is undeniable.}
{15027}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15028}{}{ENTRY #3}
{15029}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15030}{}{DATE: Classified}
{15031}{}{LOCATION: S1C}
{15032}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15033}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15034}{}{The decision to establish our operations at Hoover Dam }
{15035}{}{proves fortuitous. The region's heightened levels of }
{15036}{}{radioactive isotopes provide an ideal backdrop for our }
{15037}{}{research. Specimens thrive in this environment, }
{15038}{}{showcasing unprecedented mutations that surpass our }
{15039}{}{expectations.}
{15040}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15041}{}{ENTRY #4}
{15042}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15043}{}{DATE: Classified}
{15044}{}{LOCATION: S1C}
{15045}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15046}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15047}{}{Our creations grow to full size, a testament to the }
{15048}{}{meticulous planning and dedication of our team. Each }
{15049}{}{specimen represents a leap forward in genetic }
{15050}{}{engineering, capable of wreaking havoc on any ecosystem }
{15051}{}{it encounters. The potential for military exploitation }
{15052}{}{is staggering.}
{15053}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15054}{}{ENTRY #5}
{15055}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15056}{}{DATE: Classified}
{15057}{}{LOCATION: S1C}
{15058}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15059}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15060}{}{As our experiments progress, ethical considerations }
{15061}{}{weigh heavy on my mind. The consequences of our actions, }
{15062}{}{both intended and unintended, are profound. Yet, the }
{15063}{}{pursuit of scientific advancement drives us forward, }
{15064}{}{blurring the lines between our victory and moral }
{15065}{}{responsibility.}
{15066}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15067}{}{ENTRY #6}
{15068}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15069}{}{DATE: Classified}
{15070}{}{LOCATION: S1C}
{15071}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15072}{}{**END-PAR**}
{15073}{}{Despite the risks, we press on, fueled by the belief }
{15074}{}{that our work will make a difference on the battlefield. }
{15075}{}{The team beams with pride as we push the boundaries }
{15076}{}{of what is possible. Project Chimera represents }
{15077}{}{the pinnacle of scientific achievement, a testament }
{15078}{}{to timeless human ingenuity. Bravo, to us!}
{15079}{}{**END-DISK**}
